1
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:34,080
Bless our Yiran with smooth sailing and good fortune.

2
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:35,880
The most important thing is her happiness.

3
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:37,640
And that she stops being mad at me.

4
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:38,720
Buddha above,

5
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:42,320
please bless our Yangyang with a peaceful and happy life.

6
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:06,320
Later, we'll go get an amulet

7
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:07,680
and make an offering.

8
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:08,760
Yeah.

9
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:18,840
Hongyu,

10
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:21,160
making three wishes is usually enough.

11
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:22,680
You made way too many.

12
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,480
How can the Buddha hear them all?

13
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,360
See?

14
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,120
The Buddha even replied to you.

15
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:35,480
Every prayer is answered here.

16
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:36,440
It really works.

17
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,720
Yiran, you're not up yet?

18
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,960
The sun's already high up.

19
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:01,320
We're heading out.

20
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:01,960
Hurry up, hurry up.

21
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:03,920
I'm a little dizzy.

22
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,600
You guys go ahead. I'm not going.

23
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,920
Did you get caught in the rain last night...

24
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:09,920
...and catch a cold?

25
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,720
She really does have a bit of a fever.

26
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:15,120
She seems to have a fever.

27
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,200
Quick, come take a look.

28
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:20,720
She's burning up.

29
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:22,280
Get up, Mom will take you to the hospital.

30
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,120
I'll be fine after a nap.

31
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,520
How can you not go to the hospital?

32
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,120
You're burning up!

33
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:28,600
I'll pass out from the noise if you don't leave.

34
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:29,800
Here's the medicine.

35
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,200
I brought some medicine.

36
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:32,640
Quick, quick.

37
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:33,120
Here's some water.

38
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,680
Here, Auntie Tang brought you some medicine.

39
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:37,640
Just leave it here.

40
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:38,520
I'll take it later by myself.

41
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,640
Let Mom help you take the medicine.

42
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:40,400
Just leave it here.

43
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,160
I'll take it myself.

44
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:41,720
Wu Huilian.

45
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,520
Okay, okay, okay.

46
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:46,320
If you're feeling unwell, give us a call.

47
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,320
Okay, Auntie Tang.

48
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,200
Don't be mad.

49
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,000
It's fine.

50
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:01,680
My heart is pounding so fast.

51
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,840
We just left her all alone in the room.

52
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,200
Mr. Chen.

53
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,400
You're just in time.

54
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:09,560
Are you guys heading out?

55
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,320
Yiran, she...

56
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,080
...has a fever.

57
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,200
She's lying in bed right now.

58
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,040
And she won't let me take her to the hospital.

59
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,160
Nor will she let me stay with her.

60
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,160
Are you free right now?

61
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,200
Could you go and keep her company for me?

62
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,520
Me? I... I...

63
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,400
Why are you acting like a shy little girl?

64
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,520
Yiran is wearing a lot.

65
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,320
She's completely bundled up.

66
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:27,040
That's not what I meant.

67
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:27,520
Hurry up then.

68
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,960
Hurry up and go take care of her.

69
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:29,520
It's not appropriate for me to go.

70
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:30,240
Look, Mr. Chen.

71
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:30,960
Just go, go on.

72
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:31,920
You just...

73
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:32,440
How wonderful.

74
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,480
We're giving you young folks a chance to be alone.

75
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:35,560
I'll take good care of her.

76
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:36,800
I... I... I...

77
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,040
Yiran.

78
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:56,840
It's me.

79
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:45,960
Mr. Chen.

80
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,760
Make sure Yiran takes her medicine right away.

81
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,520
She was always getting fevers as a kid, you know?

82
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:52,840
She was in and out of the hospital constantly.

83
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:55,040
You need to make her drink more hot water.

84
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:57,440
She'll feel better after she drinks it, got it?

85
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,480
Sister Lan.

86
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,640
We're already out here.

87
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:01,800
Mr. Chen is there with her.

88
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:02,840
Don't worry.

89
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,200
Hurry up, smell this.

90
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:06,000
Doesn't it have a fresh, earthy scent?

91
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,280
It's so nice.

92
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:15,560
Let's take a picture.

93
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,400
Use your phone to take it.

94
00:07:16,400 --> 00:07:16,720
Hurry up.

95
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,560
Take a picture, come on.

96
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,280
Look here, look here.

97
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,920
Come on, tilt it down a bit.

98
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,520
One, two, three.

99
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:25,520
Looks good, right?

100
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,400
Let me see, let me see.

101
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:27,200
Let me see.

102
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,200
There's a bug!

103
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:30,640
A bug!

104
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:33,000
That scared me to death!

105
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,400
Why didn't you tell me?

106
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,080
You're terrible!

107
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,240
Let me see it.

108
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:38,960
It's so ugly.

109
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,160
What a huge mouth.

110
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,040
Delete it right now.

111
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:41,680
Delete it!

112
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,240
Delete it, delete it!

113
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,400
I won't! I won't!

114
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:44,520
What is this?

115
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:48,000
She stepped in dog poop.

116
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,040
That's so disgusting!

117
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,760
Whose dog left this poop here?

118
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,240
This is so annoying.

119
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:06,040
Seriously.

120
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,720
Sister Lan stepped in dog poop.

121
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:10,440
Maybe good luck is coming your way soon.

122
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,520
You... stay away from me.

123
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,720
It stinks!

124
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:14,840
So smelly.

125
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:17,000
Let me stink you up!

126
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:18,160
Stink you up!

127
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,200
Wait for me!

128
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,360
Come here.

129
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,680
These shoes are comfortable.

130
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:25,160
Traditional cloth shoes, so pretty.

131
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,080
See? Aren't they gorgeous?

132
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:27,080
Just now,

133
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,320
I kept hesitating.

134
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,920
I should've bought a pair too.

135
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:30,520
Exactly!

136
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:32,120
Stingy. I told you to buy them, but you didn't.

137
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:34,040
Now you missed your chance.

138
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:38,120
What's wrong?

139
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:42,680
What are you doing?

140
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,240
What's up?

141
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,240
Why do you look like you saw a debt collector?

142
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,280
What is it?

143
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:47,920
This is worse than seeing a debt collector.

144
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,520
Boss Jiang.

145
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,800
Sister Lan's romantic entanglement.

146
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:56,840
It's a small world.

147
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,520
How could we bump into him here?

148
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:01,040
Is this the young boss Sister Lan is chasing?

149
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:02,640
What do you mean I'm chasing?

150
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,440
He's chasing me!

151
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,520
Okay, okay, okay.

152
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:08,200
But let me tell you two,

153
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,720
there's absolutely nothing between us.

154
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,040
We have a comradely friendship.

155
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:11,920
Comradely friendship?

156
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:13,000
Why are you hiding in a ditch?

157
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,080
You... get out of there now.

158
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,000
We need one more.

159
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,400
Let's call him over to play mahjong.

160
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,560
Xiao Jiang!

161
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:19,840
If you yell again,

162
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,880
I'll rip off your false eyelashes

163
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:22,040
and your eyelid tape!

164
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:22,760
I mean it!

165
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:23,840
Okay, okay, okay.

166
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,160
You...

167
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:26,160
you...

168
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,680
Your hands touched dog poop!

169
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:28,960
Did you even wash them?

170
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,640
Nope.

171
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,560
Seriously.

172
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:34,680
I'm telling you,

173
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,000
she fears absolutely nothing,

174
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,480
but she's a coward when it comes to love.

175
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,360
Sister Lan,

176
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,600
at our age,

177
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:42,960
you just have to let love take its course.

178
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:43,880
What are you afraid of? Let's go.

179
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:44,600
Then you go!

180
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,920
You go chase him! You chase him!

181
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,280
Let's go.

182
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,440
Stop it.

183
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,480
Where's my scarf?

184
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,400
Your scarf.

185
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:52,120
Hurry up, let's go.

186
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:58,120
Since ancient times, love is the hardest hurdle.

187
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:00,760
Forget love? It's never that easy.

188
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:10,280
Xiao Jiang!

189
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,440
Let's play mahjong!

190
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:20,200
Keep quiet!

191
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,440
Come on, get ready to move.

192
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,760
Three, two, one, go.

193
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:37,880
I wish I could be as carefree as they are.

194
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:24,640
You're awake.

195
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,520
Why are you here?

196
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,440
Auntie Lan asked me to take care of you.

197
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,320
What are you doing?

198
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,600
Let me see if your fever broke.

199
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:44,360
It broke.

200
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:47,560
Then why is your face still red?

201
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:48,560
None of your business.

202
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,520
I'll go get you some water.

203
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,240
I'm hungry.

204
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:54,720
Let's go eat then.

205
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,520
I'll wait for you outside.

206
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:27,880
You just got over your cold.

207
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,400
Don't catch a chill.

208
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,520
Thanks.

209
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,360
What's on your mind?

210
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:50,200
Feeling guilty about something?

211
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,520
No.

212
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:54,600
What would I feel guilty about?

213
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,120
I'm in the funeral business.

214
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,320
I don't fear ghosts knocking.

215
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:58,920
Just kidding.

216
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:00,560
No need to overreact.

217
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,200
Did I?

218
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:10,680
This is really good.

219
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:13,400
Have some more.

220
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,160
You just recovered.

221
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:15,360
Thanks.

222
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:18,520
Try it.

223
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
It's delicious.

224
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,080
Go on, eat.

225
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,160
You can't even eat in peace.

226
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:34,480
What's wrong with you today?

227
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,760
Here, let me wipe your mouth.

228
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:46,360
You have a grain of rice here.

229
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:49,800
Chen Baixi.

230
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,720
Don't tell me you like me.

231
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:53,640
Yeah.

232
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,400
Are you crazy?

233
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,720
You really like me?

234
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,480
He does like you.

235
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,200
Even I could tell.

236
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:32,960
Mr. Chen...

237
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,240
I'm so disappointed in you.

238
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,560
Can't you be a little braver?

239
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,360
You're all crazy.

240
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:44,480
Yiran!

241
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:47,800
Yiran!

242
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,200
We didn't mean to follow you!

243
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,400
We just ran into you.

244
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:51,600
We messed up.

245
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,200
Why are you mad?

246
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:07,320
Here.

247
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:11,080
I got you this amulet at Daci Temple.

248
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:11,840
With this,

249
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:13,520
it will protect you and keep bad luck away.

250
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:14,440
May good luck always be with you.

251
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:18,480
It's quite pretty.

252
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:20,640
Keep it.

253
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,200
Is everything ready?

254
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,320
Didn't forget anything, right?

255
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:31,040
All good, all good.

256
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:31,800
Then let's head back.

257
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:37,480
Hongyu, I'm going to miss you so much.

258
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,040
You're leaving tomorrow.

259
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:41,080
All good things must come to an end.

260
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:43,360
Later, let's take Hongyu

261
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:45,080
to Daren's place for a big meal.

262
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:45,720
Sounds good.

263
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:46,840
I'm getting hungry anyway.

264
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,520
That's great!

265
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,080
I can finally taste the legendary

266
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,640
cooking of Wang Daren.

267
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:53,120
Let's go.

268
00:15:59,240 --> 00:15:59,800
Is this okay?

269
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:00,440
Yes, yes.

270
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,640
I'll take these to your mom.

271
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:04,400
Come on, come on.

272
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:06,040
Have some hot and fresh food.

273
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:06,880
Okay.

274
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:07,920
I'll go grill some more for you.

275
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:08,680
Sounds good.

276
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,720
Come on, girls!

277
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:11,400
Cheers!

278
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:11,880
Come on.

279
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:12,880
We won't leave until we're drunk!

280
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:22,160
Let's do it.

281
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:24,720
Here, a chicken heart as a reward.

282
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:25,800
Your favorite.

283
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:27,480
Try it.

284
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:33,120
Let me do it, let me.

285
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,040
Brother Daren.

286
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:35,640
Your cooking is amazing!

287
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,760
Eat more if you like it.

288
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:40,040
Is it okay?

289
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:40,840
Yes, yes.

290
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,480
Uncle Daren,

291
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:46,560
I brought you this.

292
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,000
You spent money again.

293
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,480
It wasn't expensive.

294
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,800
The material is really nice.

295
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:54,760
And it's thick.

296
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:55,880
What's this pattern?

297
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:56,680
It's so pretty.

298
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:57,440
Tie-dye.

299
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:58,960
I was afraid you wouldn't like it.

300
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:00,920
How could I not like it?

301
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:03,480
By the way, the leather jacket you bought me in Shanghai last year,

302
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:04,560
cost so much money.

303
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:05,720
Don't buy things like that anymore.

304
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,200
This is much more practical.

305
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,240
Okay.

306
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,040
Hang it up for me over there.

307
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:09,720
I'll wear it tomorrow.

308
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:10,640
Okay.

309
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:14,840
Has Uncle Amin been starving you these past few days?

310
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:15,640
Eat slowly.

311
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:16,600
You've got food all over your mouth.

312
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:17,720
No.

313
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:20,320
Uncle Amin is great.

314
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:22,720
Hongyu,

315
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,360
you have a boy too, right? If I remember correctly.

316
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:25,400
Yes.

317
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:27,400
That stinker of ours,

318
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:29,360
he was incredibly naughty when he was little.

319
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:31,680
One time,

320
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:34,600
he used the cushions at home as a trampoline.

321
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,040
He kept jumping on them,

322
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:38,320
until all the cotton stuffing burst out.

323
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,200
The whole room was covered in cotton.

324
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:42,360
I was so mad!

325
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:45,960
Thinking about it now,

326
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:48,760
it was actually quite cute.

327
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:51,920
Only at that age

328
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:55,720
could you do such silly things.

329
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:01,680
What's wrong?

330
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:02,680
Nothing.

331
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,640
Getting older now,

332
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,080
the wind's making my eyes water.

333
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:13,640
Auntie Tang,

334
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:15,360
I was too harsh yesterday.

335
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:17,440
I'd like to toast you.

336
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:18,200
I'm really sorry.

337
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:21,280
Sister Lan.

338
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:24,120
You see, Yiran is a good kid.

339
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:26,360
Ever since she was little, Yiran

340
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:27,840
has acted like a little adult.

341
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,200
She's so sensible.

342
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:31,920
Come on, sit down.

343
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:32,640
All right.

344
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:33,600
Have a seat.

345
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,080
Sister Lan.

346
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:39,240
To your precious daughter,

347
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:40,240
let's have a toast.

348
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:51,800
Back when we were inside,

349
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,400
what was that song we always sang?

350
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,600
Don't ask,

351
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:01,520
don't speak,

352
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:05,200
everything is understood in silence.

353
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,200
At this moment,

354
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:10,440
gathered around the candlelight,

355
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:14,320
let's spend it quietly.

356
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,800
Don't wave,

357
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:18,720
don't look back,

358
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:22,920
let me sing this song.

359
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:24,760
May your heart

360
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:29,800
forever hold my smile,

361
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:36,560
to stay with you through every season.

362
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:41,040
Parting brings sorrow,

363
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:44,800
though parting is right before us.

364
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:47,600
Saying goodbye,

365
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:51,200
but meeting again won't be too far.

366
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,920
If it's meant to be,

367
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:57,600
we can look forward to tomorrow.

368
00:19:57,600 --> 00:20:04,040
You and I will reunite in a brilliant season.

369
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:10,360
You and I will reunite in a brilliant season.

370
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:25,000
Every time I hear this song,

371
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,160
all those scenes

372
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:29,240
keep flashing before my eyes.

373
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,880
Waking up in the morning,

374
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:32,320
going to sleep at night,

375
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:34,640
running laps during the day...

376
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:35,680
These repetitive days

377
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,320
just went on and on

378
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:38,720
for eight years.

379
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:57,000
Why are we getting

380
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,320
sadder the more we drink?

381
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:00,400
To be honest,

382
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:03,160
when I first went in,

383
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,920
I was actually a bit scared.

384
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:10,840
I didn't know when I'd get out.

385
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:13,040
And I didn't know

386
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,120
how you were doing on the outside.

387
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:21,720
So I told myself,

388
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,320
"I'm already here,

389
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:26,400
so screw it."

390
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:28,440
I couldn't get out anyway.

391
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:33,440
I just treated it like three years of high school,

392
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:35,280
repeating a year,

393
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,240
and then four years of college.

394
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:38,960
And now I've finally graduated.

395
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:51,920
Have you ever regretted it?

396
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:02,560
Why would I regret it?

397
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:06,440
Regretting

398
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:12,560
is just bullying your past self.

399
00:22:14,440 --> 00:22:16,560
When you made that decision,

400
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:20,520
you must have made the best choice at the time.

401
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:22,160
You had no other options.

402
00:22:22,280 --> 00:22:23,800
You were at a dead end.

403
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:26,440
That's the only reason you'd make a choice like that.

404
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:30,600
Now,

405
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:32,240
it's too late for me to regret it anyway.

406
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:33,840
I'll just take it as it comes.

407
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:34,600
You know?

408
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,120
It's no big deal.

409
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:38,640
It's no big deal.

410
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:42,080
When your heart is big, your problems become small.

411
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:43,360
Right, Zhang Lijuan?

412
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:44,520
Isn't that right, Tang Hongyu?

413
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:45,320
Sister Lan,

414
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:48,920
Meeting you in this lifetime

415
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:50,440
was totally worth it.

416
00:22:50,600 --> 00:22:51,720
Just for that,

417
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:52,680
come on.

418
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:55,200
Bottoms up!

419
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:56,400
Grab your bottles and chug!

420
00:23:08,880 --> 00:23:10,120
Way to go, Sister Lan.

421
00:23:11,320 --> 00:23:12,640
Yangyang!

422
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:14,680
Watch your Godmother put on a show for you.

423
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:16,280
One...

424
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:18,000
Two...

425
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:19,520
Three!

426
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:48,800
You two are way out of line.

427
00:23:50,920 --> 00:23:52,400
What if Pops were here?

428
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:53,560
B-Brother-in-law.

429
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,440
It's pitch black. What are you doing?

430
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:58,560
You scared me to death!

431
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:01,920
Sorry about that, Brother-in-law.

432
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:02,680
I didn't know you were home.

433
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:04,000
Xiaofang.

434
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:05,960
How about we go somewhere else?

435
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:09,240
Some people are just jealous.

436
00:24:12,320 --> 00:24:13,520
I've been away for a couple of days.

437
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:15,560
And you guys don't even care.

438
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:16,640
Why should we care?

439
00:24:16,800 --> 00:24:18,520
It's not like you'd get lost.

440
00:24:18,520 --> 00:24:21,520
Then why don't you ask me what I lost?

441
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:27,000
Bro.

442
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,800
Don't tell me you lost...

443
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:30,040
Wait a second.

444
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:31,960
This calls for a drink.

445
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,400
Drunk words are sober thoughts. Wait here.

446
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,280
Is it what I think it is?

447
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:42,200
We'll talk in a bit.

448
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:43,280
The drinks aren't ready yet.

449
00:24:54,840 --> 00:24:55,360
Bro.

450
00:24:56,320 --> 00:24:57,240
Actually, I know.

451
00:24:57,240 --> 00:25:00,160
You staying at Paradise Funeral Home is partly because of Yiran.

452
00:25:01,640 --> 00:25:03,760
We came from the same womb.

453
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:05,240
We have a bit of a telepathic connection.

454
00:25:05,360 --> 00:25:07,800
Fan Shiqi is such an outstanding rich girl,

455
00:25:07,800 --> 00:25:09,760
and you didn't even give her a second look.

456
00:25:10,360 --> 00:25:12,560
But when you heard Yiran wasn't returning to Shanghai,

457
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:15,200
you were over the moon.

458
00:25:16,360 --> 00:25:17,520
I'm happy. Of course I'm happy.

459
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:19,760
She's our friend, isn't she?

460
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:21,520
Of course I'd be happy that she's staying.

461
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:22,320
Don't give me that.

462
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:24,320
I'll just tell you one thing.

463
00:25:24,480 --> 00:25:25,800
In this lifetime,

464
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:28,800
how many people can you truly love?

465
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:29,920
Very few.

466
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:30,960
No.

467
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:32,320
Only one.

468
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:35,240
If, say,

469
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:37,640
Yiran finds a new boyfriend,

470
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:38,880
or if

471
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:42,120
she meets another scumbag like Zhuang Qiang,

472
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:44,160
would you regret it?

473
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:45,080
I would.

474
00:25:45,080 --> 00:25:46,240
I d-definitely would.

475
00:25:47,160 --> 00:25:48,600
The fact that you like Yiran...

476
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:50,160
except for Yiran herself,

477
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:52,160
we all know it perfectly well.

478
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:55,800
From high school until now,

479
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,360
you've finally crossed paths again.

480
00:25:57,360 --> 00:26:00,840
How could you bear to let her slip away again?

481
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:06,240
Xiaofang is right.

482
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:10,960
You only live once.

483
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:12,840
You shouldn't leave any regrets.

484
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:16,800
Then why haven't you found someone else?

485
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:17,800
You...

486
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:22,320
I just haven't had the chance yet!

487
00:26:23,440 --> 00:26:24,400
Pops!

488
00:26:24,920 --> 00:26:26,560
Alright, I'll leave you two to it.

489
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:38,560
Auntie Tang.

490
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:39,680
Have some tea.

491
00:26:40,720 --> 00:26:41,560
Careful.

492
00:26:45,200 --> 00:26:46,800
Drinking all by yourselves?

493
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:48,320
And you didn't invite me?

494
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:49,680
What's the big idea?

495
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:52,960
Hot, hot, hot!

496
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,520
Hot!

497
00:26:54,960 --> 00:26:55,960
Are you okay, Auntie?

498
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:00,400
Alright.

499
00:27:00,400 --> 00:27:01,200
Old Li.

500
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:02,480
It's so hot, Old Li.

501
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:03,640
Alright, come back.

502
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:05,560
Old Li, come down and drink with me.

503
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:06,520
No need to come down.

504
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:07,360
Here.

505
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:08,560
Why are you back out here?

506
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:10,360
Careful, careful, careful.

507
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:11,200
I want another drink.

508
00:27:11,200 --> 00:27:11,960
Careful.

509
00:27:13,880 --> 00:27:15,520
So hot, so hot.

510
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:18,640
Are you okay, Auntie Tang?

511
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:19,440
I'm fine.

512
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:21,160
Sorry you had to see that.

513
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:23,120
It's fine.

514
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:28,160
Yiran.

515
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:32,920
Don't mind me nagging.

516
00:27:33,400 --> 00:27:34,720
You and Sister Lan...

517
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:37,000
You both care about each other deep down.

518
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,480
From now on, whatever is on your mind,

519
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:40,000
don't keep it bottled up.

520
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:43,240
Mother and son...

521
00:27:47,680 --> 00:27:49,640
Mother and daughter share a heart.

522
00:27:49,640 --> 00:27:51,520
Everything will be fine if you talk it out.

523
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:53,440
I know.

524
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:55,920
I know you want the best for us.

525
00:27:56,640 --> 00:27:57,760
Thank you, Auntie Tang.

526
00:27:57,760 --> 00:27:59,120
That puts my mind at ease.

527
00:27:59,880 --> 00:28:00,680
Time for bed.

528
00:28:03,520 --> 00:28:04,640
Time for bed.

529
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:26,800
Good night.

530
00:28:27,320 --> 00:28:28,120
Good night.

531
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:29,240
Go to sleep.

532
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:32,440
Get some rest.

533
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:34,440
Go to sleep.

534
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:42,440
Tang Hongyu

535
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:49,160
Tang Hongyu

536
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:53,920
She won't be leaving anymore.

537
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:10,600
Sister Lan, I'm heading out.

538
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:14,440
You drank too much last night.

539
00:31:14,440 --> 00:31:16,000
You were sleeping so soundly,

540
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:17,640
so I didn't wake you up.

541
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:49,880
I left secretly,

542
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:51,120
without even saying a word.

543
00:31:54,440 --> 00:31:56,240
I made some hangover soup for you.

544
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:57,400
Remember to drink it.

545
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:01,360
Take better care of yourself and drink less.

546
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:02,800
You're so thoughtful.

547
00:32:02,800 --> 00:32:04,480
Drinking too much is bad for your stomach.

548
00:32:04,480 --> 00:32:05,360
You hear me?

549
00:32:09,080 --> 00:32:12,120
Try not to argue with Yiran so much.

550
00:32:12,120 --> 00:32:16,000
You both have such straightforward personalities.

551
00:32:16,320 --> 00:32:17,920
But I can tell.

552
00:32:17,920 --> 00:32:20,640
Deep down, she really cares about you.

553
00:32:20,640 --> 00:32:21,440
So from now on,

554
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:23,160
be a bit more patient with her.

555
00:32:24,360 --> 00:32:26,400
She's your own daughter.

556
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,960
Your own flesh and blood.

557
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:30,400
I know she's my own flesh and blood. You don't have to tell me.

558
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:32,560
Sister Lan.

559
00:32:33,280 --> 00:32:36,920
You should plan for your own future too.

560
00:32:37,720 --> 00:32:39,080
At your age,

561
00:32:39,080 --> 00:32:41,680
it's not easy finding someone suitable.

562
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:44,920
I think... Boss Jiang from yesterday,

563
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:46,840
he's pretty nice.

564
00:32:46,840 --> 00:32:49,360
You two could look out for each other in the future.

565
00:32:49,360 --> 00:32:50,320
And your days...

566
00:32:50,320 --> 00:32:52,080
would be a bit more comfortable.

567
00:32:52,400 --> 00:32:54,800
You're meddling way too much.

568
00:32:58,320 --> 00:32:59,160
I don't need to look for anyone.

569
00:32:59,680 --> 00:33:00,520
Sister Lan.

570
00:33:01,600 --> 00:33:04,080
Thank you for your hospitality these past few days.

571
00:33:05,040 --> 00:33:07,120
You and Sister Juan are both good people.

572
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:08,920
These past few days,

573
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:11,440
I've been really happy.

574
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:14,480
Out of the months since I got out,

575
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:16,640
these were the happiest days.

576
00:33:19,840 --> 00:33:21,400
My whole life,

577
00:33:22,040 --> 00:33:23,320
toiling away.

578
00:33:24,520 --> 00:33:25,480
I've had a hard life.

579
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:31,320
My mind was always on three meals a day.

580
00:33:31,840 --> 00:33:33,520
Providing for my family.

581
00:33:35,120 --> 00:33:37,520
For my parents' health.

582
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:40,600
For Hualin to grow up safely.

583
00:33:41,880 --> 00:33:43,440
I lived desperately.

584
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:49,360
But honestly, even now, I'm not sure...

585
00:33:50,560 --> 00:33:52,400
what it was all for.

586
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:57,360
Sister Lan.

587
00:33:58,200 --> 00:34:00,240
By the time you hear this message,

588
00:34:00,640 --> 00:34:02,320
I'll already be gone.

589
00:34:04,520 --> 00:34:06,800
This is the last time I'll talk to you.

590
00:34:11,160 --> 00:34:13,000
Don't cry too hard.

591
00:34:14,440 --> 00:34:15,920
And don't be too sad.

592
00:34:17,480 --> 00:34:19,440
I should have listened to you.

593
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:23,080
And left a larger offering at the temple.

594
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:26,840
Maybe down there now,

595
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:29,520
I'd still be bargaining with the King of Hell.

596
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:32,680
To get...

597
00:34:33,160 --> 00:34:36,120
a chance to reincarnate into a rich family.

598
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:40,000
So my next life might be a bit easier.

599
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:45,360
And also,

600
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:48,920
the world is so big.

601
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:54,040
There are so many places I've never been.

602
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:58,920
So much good food I've never eaten.

603
00:35:00,880 --> 00:35:02,040
So for me,

604
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:05,120
keep living happily.

605
00:35:06,160 --> 00:35:08,720
Be happy for me.

606
00:35:08,720 --> 00:35:09,520
Okay?

607
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:10,560
Li Yiran!

608
00:35:11,040 --> 00:35:12,240
Li Yiran!

609
00:35:27,680 --> 00:35:28,720
Don't worry.

610
00:35:29,880 --> 00:35:31,120
I'll be up in heaven,

611
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:32,960
watching over you.

612
00:36:05,960 --> 00:36:07,080
Alright.

613
00:36:07,880 --> 00:36:09,440
Let's not say goodbye.

614
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:12,160
Take care.

615
00:36:36,920 --> 00:36:38,080
Hello?

616
00:36:39,360 --> 00:36:39,800
Hello.

617
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:40,960
Is this Wu Huilian?

618
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:41,560
Yes.

619
00:36:41,560 --> 00:36:42,920
This is the police station.

620
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:45,400
This morning, on a suburban railway line,

621
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:47,000
we found a woman's body.

622
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:49,760
Her ID says her name is Tang Hongyu.

623
00:36:49,760 --> 00:36:52,000
The last call record on her phone

624
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:53,240
is your phone number.

625
00:36:53,680 --> 00:36:55,760
Um, based on the scene,

626
00:36:55,760 --> 00:36:56,600
our preliminary conclusion

627
00:36:56,600 --> 00:36:58,000
is suicide by train.

628
00:36:58,000 --> 00:36:58,640
So,

629
00:36:58,640 --> 00:37:01,240
we need you at the station to assist the investigation.

630
00:37:01,240 --> 00:37:02,960
When would you be free to come over?

631
00:37:05,320 --> 00:37:05,680
Hello?

632
00:37:05,680 --> 00:37:06,520
What happened?

633
00:37:06,520 --> 00:37:07,200
Easy, easy.

634
00:37:07,200 --> 00:37:08,000
Let's get you up.

635
00:37:10,800 --> 00:37:11,480
Thank you.

636
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:14,120
You have such great taste.

637
00:38:14,120 --> 00:38:16,800
I loved wearing this little red flower when I was young.

638
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:19,040
So pretty.

639
00:38:40,600 --> 00:38:41,760
Where are my mom's things?

640
00:38:41,760 --> 00:38:42,760
Where are my mom's things?

641
00:38:49,080 --> 00:38:50,080
Hualin.

642
00:38:50,560 --> 00:38:51,560
Hualin.

643
00:38:52,280 --> 00:38:53,280
Hualin.

644
00:38:59,840 --> 00:39:02,360
I... I'm Wu Huilian.

645
00:39:02,640 --> 00:39:04,160
Your mom's cellmate.

646
00:39:04,960 --> 00:39:07,440
I saw you when we first got out of prison.

647
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:11,960
I'm sorry.

648
00:39:12,720 --> 00:39:14,200
It's all my fault.

649
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:17,200
I didn't take good care of your mom.

650
00:39:32,560 --> 00:39:33,760
And this.

651
00:39:43,120 --> 00:39:44,080
Child,

652
00:39:45,240 --> 00:39:46,840
If you want to cry,

653
00:39:46,840 --> 00:39:48,440
don't hold it in.

654
00:39:49,080 --> 00:39:50,440
Just let it out.

655
00:39:50,440 --> 00:39:52,240
Why should I cry?

656
00:39:52,240 --> 00:39:53,320
Why should I cry?

657
00:39:53,920 --> 00:39:54,640
You...

658
00:39:55,480 --> 00:39:56,360
His mom just passed away.

659
00:39:56,360 --> 00:39:58,240
It's normal to be emotional.

660
00:40:00,560 --> 00:40:02,200
Why should I cry?

661
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:03,840
Why should I cry?

662
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:20,200
Why did she leave?

663
00:40:20,200 --> 00:40:22,440
Why did she do this?

664
00:40:28,280 --> 00:40:30,840
Why did she do this?

665
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:47,000
But why?

666
00:41:26,840 --> 00:41:28,360
The sun is setting.

667
00:41:29,080 --> 00:41:30,480
We've been standing here all afternoon.

668
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:33,480
Let's go back.

669
00:41:39,640 --> 00:41:41,040
I just don't understand

670
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:45,720
why she has to act like this.

671
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:50,840
She didn't even say hello when she came.

672
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:55,800
And she didn't say a word when she left.

673
00:41:58,280 --> 00:42:00,120
When we were in prison,

674
00:42:01,120 --> 00:42:04,360
our only hope was to live a good life once we got out.

675
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:06,960
We finally made it out,

676
00:42:12,240 --> 00:42:15,280
so there must be something she just can't get over.
